  "note": "Machine-readable snapshot of the curated public API. Generated from the installed package; tests/packaging/test_public_api.py asserts equality. ReadinessTarget/RequirementClass are reused from ugence-uvi-policy-contracts. GateResult embeds a PolicyGate (kind/applicability derived, not caller-set); blocking/indeterminate gate ids are derived properties of the determination, not fields. GV-3R-b adds the single canonical evaluator entry point evaluate_readiness(case, *, evaluation_time): ReadinessEvaluationCase carries NO classification field \u2014 the evaluator selects the tier \u2014 and ReadinessEvaluationResult is advisory, never a deployment authorization. Readiness requirements are policy/gate-driven: indicator records are diagnostics, not a global prerequisite. The governing ReadinessPolicy's lifecycle state and effective period are evaluated as ADR \u00a76 precondition row 0 at the explicit evaluation_time. GV-3R-c adds the single canonical trusted orchestration boundary assess_readiness(request, *, policy_resolver, gate_verifier, condition_verifier) around that one evaluator \u2014 no second classification algorithm exists. Every injected boundary defaults to None, which DENIES: the exact ReadinessPolicy must resolve through the shared Ugence Policy Authority's public resolution service, and only independently verified gate results and conditions reach the evaluator. ReadinessAssessmentRequest carries no classification, no trust boolean, no policy body and no financial field; ReadinessAssessmentOutcome is advisory, unsigned, and authorizes_deployment is a permanently-False property, not a field. No allow-all or testing verifier is exported \u2014 that absence is the boundary.",
